YAFAP [S] Twurckle lycanthropic rogue, genoless
 
I finally did it, my first ascension!! 
After playing nethack and slashem for nearly two years, Twurckle the
male chaotic lycanthropic rogue finally ascended to demigod status
(slashem 7e2). He managed to keep genoless conduct and did not use
Elbereth. He also didn't polymorph objects, but doing so is useless
anyhow in slash'em.
Here is a *very* long and spoily post about his adventure.

Lycanthropy had slowly driven twurckle to madness.. for years he had
tried to fight it, but to no avail. The town healer had suggested all
kinds of things.. wolfsbane, prayer... but nothing worked, his case of
lycanthropy seemed to be special, and incurable.
Finally one night, at full moon, he lost his last bit of sanity and
ran of into the night towards the entrance of the dungeons that had
haunted his werefeverish dreams for years.

Twurckle entered the dungeon and found himself in a small dusty room,
the room was empty except for some pieces of armor next to an old
rotten door. Twurckle examined the armor and put it on and found out
they were a +4 pair of gauntlets of dexterity and a +1 banded mail!
(high dexterity improves your AC in slashem, making GoD very, very
usefull). Twurckle grinned from ear to ear when he realized what he
had just found, but then he suddenly felt his entire body starting to
itch.. Because he had years of experience with lycanthropy he managed
to quickly remove his clothing before the change would rip them
appart.
Hair started growing everywhere, his body morphed into the shape of a
wolf, and his feral instincts took over.

He nearly collapsed under the suddenly heavy load and was forced to
drop most of his items. Even though he could barely think straight his
instincts told him the gloves where important, as well as his blessed
scrolls of teleportation and his lockpick, being a rogue he kept his
gold. he dropped everything else, howled one last time at the moon
that shone through the dungeon's entrance, and ran of into the
darkness.
He had a strange feeling that the RNG was mocking him by putting all
the nice armor in the first room, knowing that Twurckle would not be
able to use it.
Somewhat grumpy Twurckle explored the first level of the strange
dungeon and found a unalligned, lawful altar, a sink, and one object
that intrigued him more than everything else: A toilet! His canine
instincts took over and unable to control himself he ran towards it
and started drinking.
"The toilet water is quite refreshing!"
After drinking a bit more he noticed no obvious other effects and
continued exploring.
He found a total of four sinks on the first three levels, Some weird
feeling (must be his instincts again) told Twurckle that he had to
find a way to control his lycanthropy, and that the item needed, a
ring of polymorph control might be obtained from sinks.
(As a lycanthrope you spend around 90 percent of your time in
wolf-form untill you find some means of polymorph control, if you die
in wolven form you return to human form, with less than half of your
hitpoints, and a high chance of losing maxHP. While in wolf-form
you're not able to wear armor, or cary more then a few basic items,
this is no big problem in the early game, but you have to find a way
to control your lycanthropy sooner or later, or the lack of magic
resistance (difficult to acquire without armor) or the inability to
wield weapons will get you killed.

Twurckle, still in wolven form and thus not too bright, figured he
could outrun anything that came from a sink, (the stairs were 2
squares away) He kicked the sink, and a beautifull young succubus
appeared. Twurckle gazed at her in amazement and forgot to run away.
The succubus did not seem to like furry animals, and destroyed
twurckles wolf form in a single hit.
Twurckle awoke in serious pain from his lycanthropic fit, he did not
remember much from what happened while he was in wolf form, but he
vaguely recalled drinking from a toilet. He had not much time to
gather his memory, as he found himself on the dungeon floor,
completely naked, with a very attractive succubus (that must have been
as suprised as Twurckle) kneeled over him.
Strangely the succubus did not seem to mind Twurckles toilet-breath,
and she seemed to enjoy the experience more than him. Twurckle was
left with his power drained. (lycanthropes have intrinsic level drain
resistance, I could have been dead otherwise) Lycantrophy kicked in
again several turns later, and twurckle was more carefull with the
other sinks, he killed any black puddings and succubi, and got the
four rings. none of them was polymorph control, but he did get a ring
of warning. Some levels where gained and Twurckle could now summon
wolves at the cost of 10 Pw, or change between wolven and human form
for 10 pw (it's not practical to try and stay in human form, you'll
polymorph back too often and you'll quickly run out of power) A small
pack of wolves, including a winter wolf was summoned. He named the
winter wolf Frostbite.

Twurckle entered the gnomish mines, hungry for food. (lycanthropes
have intrinsic regeneration, which is extremely usefull, but it's not
hungerless, so you need a *lot* of food). Frostbite and his other pets
kept the gnomes and dwarves at a safe distance, but Twurckle stepped
on a landmine on the third level of the mines, and got his wolven form
destroyed again..
There was a nasty dwarf with a wand of polymorph on the same level,
that zapped itself in komodo dragon form, orange jelly form, and when
those forms where killed into an asassin bug. (monsters change back to
their original form in [S] when you destroy their polymorphed form)
Twurckle managed to flee from the asassin bug using a scroll of
teleportation. He finally made it to gnometown, the temple was
unaligned, but he found a magic whistle in a shop, and a (cursed)
magic lamp! He bought the magic whistle, put the lamp into a bag, and
instructed Frostbite to steal it.

Twurckle realized he needed to make holy water to use the magic lamp,
and started to move up to level 1 which had an unattended altar. This
meant he had to pass the assasin bug dwarf again.. He did want to keep
his last blessed scroll of teleportation for the altar conversion
(lawful gods like to sent down monadic deva's and other angelic types
if their altars are converted) and since the foul creature was almost
on the other side of the level he decided to try and outrun it.
Twurckle and his pack of wolves ran for their lives, but the assasin
bug caught up with them right before the stairs, and it destroyed
Twurckles wolven form in two bites. Twurckle immediately #youpolyed
back into a wolf for the extra hitpoints, made it to the stairs, got
his wolven form destroyed *again*, but managed to climb the stairs
with a few remaining hitpoints.. He realized that, had he not been a
lycanthrope, he would have YASD't a lot of times by now.. (I think
lycanthropes are greatly underestimated by many people)

Twurckle managed to convert the altar on the third try, without any
angels showing up, made holy water, and wished for a ring of polymorph
control. Finally the cure to his lycanthropy! He had been embaressed
way too often by waking up from another lycanthropic session with his
head stuck in a toilet.
He put on the ring, morphed back to human form, and got in his armor.
He sacrificed a bit more and got the bat from hell. suddenly his life
looked a lot better.
Twurckle went back down into the mines, killed the assasin bug/dwarf
and took his wand of polymorph, his human form had sustained severe
maxhitpoint damage during all the early game accidents, so he zapped
the wand at himself and became a new lycanthrope, which raised his max
hitpoints from 42 to 58, even though he lost three experience levels
(now level 5) the leveldrain also meant that He suddenly could afford
to buy protection (bought three points)
AC was now -16 :). 

Twurckle descended to the bottom of the mines (vampires level) and
continued deeper to Ruggo's level, and was greeted on the stairs by an
gnomish wizard with a wand of sleep, he put Twurckle to sleep for an
eternity, but was unable to do much damage. Twurckle killed him and
took his wand of sleep, when Ruggo the gnomeking came around the
corner and zapped poor Twurckle with another wand of sleep. he nearly
got killed, and woke up just in time. Somewhat impressed, Twurckle
fled back up the stairs with the help of a blessed scroll of teleport
but there was a gnome warrior waiting around the corner *WITH A WAND
OF SLEEP*. the sleepray bounced of the wall and put the gnome to sleep
as well, and Twurckle woke up sooner than the gnome. But the RNG had
made his point clear, and Twurckle decided to avoid the level untill
he had sleep resistance. sjeez..

Twurckle decided to explore the main dungeon, and found that there was
a small village with shops on dlvl 6, the stores had 2 magic markers,
a bag of holding, a magic candle, jumping boots and a drum! (usefull
for scaring monsters, and getting backstab bonusses) Frostbite stole
them for him.
Twurckle collected all the daggers from the mines, cancelled them,
dipped them in a potion of gain level, and enchanted them to +7, which
gave him a stack of 36 +7 elven daggers (stashed 20 of them)
Next was sokoban, somehow Twurckle magically remembered the solutions
to all the puzzles (must be his wolven instinct again), but on the
third level he encountered some nasty monsters. He took his drum,
intending to scare them, so he could easily stab them down from behind
(he was an evil rogue after all) but this proved to be unwise. he
played the drum and got a message like "The entire dungeon shakes
around you" the entire level was suddenly filled with pits and
craters, and the level was rendered completely unsolvable (The drum
appeared to be a drum of earthquake, I didn't even know they existed
:-( )

Twurckle gave up on finishing sokoban, returned to the main dungeon,
found a dead end corridor, reverse genocided gray dragons and killed
them with a deadly rain of +7 elven daggers. He got two sets of
scales, and not much later he had his GDSM.

Twurckle was still very upset about finding this new and exiting way
to mess up sokoban, and ran back to Ruggo the Gnomeking, and massacred
him and all his gnomish friends out of pure frustration (He now had
sleep resistance).
He continued descending in the main dungeon, and did the same to the
Rat king and Grund the orc king and friends. Things got a bit out of
hand there when an orc started zapping a wand of summon horde. There
were so many orcs that he was completely clueless on who the cullprit
was, and when he finally killed the right orc the wand was empty and
over half the level was filled with monsters. Twurckle enjoyed the
slaughter though, and after he was done he had calmed down a bit. He
had gained teleport control and teleportritis from some of the victims
of the battle. Two traumatised nurses walked through the devastated
wasteland searching the hundreds of charred corpses looking for
survivors, but there were none but Twurckle, and since he was the only
survivor they did not mind giving him some "healing". He got 16hp.
He also found a wand of wishing, but decided he would not use more
wishes than the one he had used so far.

Twurckle entered the quest, and visited his old master. The man
insulted Twurckle in many ways and demanded that Twurckle was to
immediately retrieve the master key of thievery for him. Twurckle
decided to do the quest, but that he would keep the artifact himself.
He continued to the bottom of the quest, polymorphed into a xorn and
killed the master assasin. The polymorph timed out, as expected, and
it left Twurckle stranded in one of the larger rooms with no way to
the exit.

He thought he was prepared and read two cursed scrolls of teleport,
when asked what level to teleport to he answered 17 to the first and
12 to the second scroll but it did not work.. (I posted to the
newsgroup and it probably had something to do with the levels of the
quest having their own numbering from 1 to 5) He decided to wrest the
last charge from his wand of polymorph, and tried to polymorph into a
xorn, but the polymorph failed (the change it works seems to be less
than 100%) So now he was stranded at the bottom of the quest with no
way out, no blank scrolls, no way of polymorphing, no scrolls of
teleportor unholy water..
He waited for approximately 12.000 turns and nearly quit the game in
pure frustration, but finally a chameleon on the other side of the
level polymorphed into a master lich, teleported next to twurckle,
summoned some nasties, polymorphed into someting innocent, got killed
and left a corpse. Twurckle ate the corpse, polymorphed into a xorn
and escaped.

He did the other quests without much trouble, but failed to get
nightmares horn, he wacked her with a cockatrice corpse and the horn
was seemingly destroyed in the process. Finally he made it to a
magical portal on level 22 which brought him to a truly enormous shop,
as big as the entire level, and about half filled with all kinds of
equipment. Ms. One-eyed Sam did not appear to like Twurckle though,
and she asked truly ridiculous prices
"That's only 1600 zorkmids for this food ration" 
Twurckle dragged all the usefull items to a corner of the store,
alchemized and got 32 potions of holy water, and potions worth 41
hitpoints and 22 power, he enchanted most of his armor and ate several
food rations, and picked up speed boots and a ring of conflict,
meanwhile one eyed Sam was loudly announcing the ridiculous prices for
all the items. After taking all interesting items he walked over to
one-eyed sam and asked her how high the bill was:
"One-eyed Sam says that your bill comes to 2084510 zorkmids"
Twurckle checked his belongings, saw that he had only 356 zorkmids,
walked to the corner of the shop, polymorphed into a xorn and xorned
through the wall, leaving Ms. One-eyed Sam behind.

Twurckle found the portal to Ludios on dlvl 39, he managed to get tons
and tons of loot (and yet another wand of wishing). He had to walk all
the way back to minetown which had the only peacefull priest of the
game to buy his last protection, the other priests were all unfriendly
priests of moloch, and there was some insane, evil priest in the
lawful quest.
He took some of the bullets from Ludios and returned to One-eyed Sams
market. She was still screaming about the theft and threatening to
kill everything and everyone. Twurckle helped her out of her misery by
gunning her down twice. She had a +4 shield of reflection, and +3
speed boots.
(The latest version of slashem seems to have balanced firearms
somewhat, bullets get destroyed by grenade explosions and fire which
means that they have become somewhat rare, but firearms are still way
overpowered, I only used them for Sam, who killed more of my promising
characters than I want to remember)

He was now ready to enter gehennom. He had cleaned the dungeon as deep
as level 43 which was Medusa's level and had an AC of aproximately -50
and 345 hitpoints. An amulet of flying completed his ascension kit
(there are some nasty slashem spells that make flying or water walking
a critical ascension kit item. the pool of water spell was used at
least five times in this game, mostly in situations where I was
surrounded)

But then disaster struck.

In his greed Twurckle had become careless and opened a chest without
checking it for traps, he was jolted by a massive surge of
electricity, which destroyed his ring of polymorph control, his ring
of free action and his only wand of teleportation (the first wand of
teleportation in this game was generated on level 37, there were even
more wands of wishing in the game :-/ ) He had a backup for the ring
of free action but not for his polymorph control, Which meant he once
again had uncontrolled lycanthropy, which at this depth and stage of
the game would probably mean death within several hundreds of turns.
He had always feared this would happen though, and had found another
possible but quite radical cure: a potion of vampire blood. His
"instincts" told him that drinking it would polymorph him into a
vampire, with no polymorph timeout.
He morphed into a vampire with 41 max hitpoints.
Vampires have many advantages and disadvantages, many of which are
shared with lycanthropes (intrinsic regeneration, level drain
resistance) but they also have other nice intrinsics such as intrinsic
flying and magical breathing. Their biggest disadvantage is that they
can't eat, but get hungry incredibly fast. They can suck blood from
victims, and corpses that are no older than two or three turns, but it
is far less effective than normal food. Twurckle already had a ring of
slow digestion so that was not wat he was worried about. He only had
41 hitpoints, and at the depth where he was there were plenty of
creatures that would happily deal that kind of damage in a single
turn, and destruction of his vampiric form would mean he would be back
to uncontrolled lycanthropy. It also meant he could not pray for the
rest of the game, because Kos would probably be "helpfull", and cure
him out of his polymorphed state.

Twurckle managed to get back to sokoban in one piece, where he was
painfully reminded of how he had completely messed up that part of the
game.... But he thought he could make use of the relatively safe
location. He stripped down naked, unwielded his weapon and read three
cursed scrolls of genocide. 15 nurses were summoned. Twurckle had the
time of his life, he definitely had never been this popular as a
lycanthrope. His hitpoints were raised to 214. He replaced his amulet
of flying (wich he now had as an intrinsic) with a amulet vs stoning.
(cockatrices are very dangerous for a vampire, you can't eat lizard
corpses, and you have a bite attack, which makes accidents far more
likely) AC was -59! (being a vampire seemed to have lowered his
natural armor class by quite a lot)

Twurckle now felt save enough to enter gehennom, and things went quite
smoothly, he gathered some potions of blood from other vampires in the
valley of the death, which meant he had a small safeguard against
starvation. Demogorgon was killed with a cockatrice corpse, and the
amulet vs stoning proved it's worth. Demogorgon summoned a succubus in
his last turn, which immediately seduced Twurckles gloves off while
Twurckle was not paying attention because he was trying to save
himself from dying of illness. The other demon lords were no problem,
nor was Vlad the Impaler.
Level 61, an icemaze, seemed to be the deepest level of the dungeon,
He found the vibrating square on a patch of ice, and marked it by
reading a scroll of light.

After this Twurckle went back up to kill the wizard, he managed to
reach the top of the wizard's tower without much trouble. Only one of
his predecessors had come this far, Urrberup, a caveman had made it to
the tower, and had sneeked up on the wizard, planning to wack him on
the head with a cockatrice corpse, but he had forgotten to check
wether he was still wearing his gloves. The wizard of Yendor was still
smiling about it)
The Wizard died with this smile upon his face when Twurckle shot him
with a wand of death. Twurckle knew (his instincts again) that he had
to do something with certain items on the vibrating square to
continue, but it was a huge mess and it took a while before he got the
sequence right (The Icy vibrating square was turned into water by a
series of accidents, which got twurckle all nervous, but it still
seemed to work. The whole transformation of the dungeon was a very
cool effect, though the messages said something about walls crumbling
while there where no walls, just ice)
The battle at Molochs sanctum was huge.. Twurckles hitpoints slowly
decreased, and things looked very bad, each monster he killed seemed
to get replaced by a stronger enemy. Twurckle finally remembered he
had a ring of conflict, which made things a lot easier. He killed the
high priest and finally for the first time ever had the amulet!

Next came the run back up the stairs, The wizard showed up on level
57, the castle, 30 and 15, and earth. Twurckle seemed to be completely
unable to zap him with the wand of death, which was dodged every time
since the first encounter in the wizard's tower, so he had to kill him
the old-fashioned way. Twurckle was so exited about the whole amulet
of yendor thing that he made a near-fatal mistake, he had forgotten to
put his ring of slow digestion back on after he had replaced it with
the ring of conflict. He didn't notice untill he suddenly fainted. He
had some potions of blood, which appeared to have almost no
nutritionall value, he only got back to weak status, but a helpfull
black dragon was drained of blood, and twurckle survived. He finally
made it to the planes, Earth, Air, Fire and Water were all
ridiculously easy (used gold detection), Water was weird though with
the whole strange bubble things. Twurckle never lost more than 30
hitpoints, but he was getting incredibly scared about having to face
Famine, he only had a few potions of blood to satisfy his hunger, and
he knew from his earlier experience that they barely helped. After
getting satiated by lingering on water to drain some extra creatures
he stepped through the portal to Astral.

You activated a magic portal! You feel dizzy for a moment but the
sensation passes. You
arrive on the Astral Plane! Here the High temples of the aligned gods
are located.
You sense alarm, hostility and excitement in the air! A voice
whispers: "Thou hast been
worthy of me!" An angel appears near you. 

Twurckle ignored the angel, and continued on his quest, somehow Death
was already awake without Twurckle doing anything, so twurckle choose
to fight him first, he had preferred to fight Pestilence first as his
"instincts" told him Death was quite scary. Death approached Twurckle
and touched poor Twurckle with his deadly Touch. Both Death and
Twurckle were very suprised when nothing happened.. absolutely
nothing.. just some message like "was that the touch of Death?"
Twurckle was quite happy about discovering yet another advantage of
being a vampire and attacked Death, he died in TWO HITS!! Was this the
great Death that he had heard so much about? Twurckle continued
towards the altar, humiliated Death a second time and found that the
altar belonged to Kos. After checking and double checking that Kos was
indeed his god he sacrificed the amulet:

You offer the Amulet of Yendor to Kos... An Invisible choir sings, and
you are bathed in
radiance... The voice of Kos thunders:" Congratulations, mortal!"
"In return for thy service, I grant thee the gift of immortality!" You
ascend to the status
of Demigod...

